.TH SWANCTL 8 "2026-09-15" "@PACKAGE_VERSION@" "strongSwan"
.SH NAME
swanctl \- strongSwan configuration, control and monitoring command line interface.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY "swanctl"
.I command
.RI [ option\~ .\|.\|.]
.YS
.
.SY "swanctl"
.B \-h
|
.B \-\-help
.YS
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
swanctl is a cross-platform command line utility to configure, control and
monitor the strongSwan IKE daemon. It is a replacement for the deprecated
.BR starter ,
.B ipsec
and
.B stroke
tools.

swanctl uses a configuration file called
.BR swanctl.conf (5)
to parse configurations and credentials. Private keys, certificates and other
PKI related credentials are read from specific directories (see DIRECTORIES
below).

To communicate with the IKE daemon, swanctl uses the VICI protocol, the
Versatile IKE Configuration Interface. This stable interface is usable by
other tools and is often preferable than scripting swanctl and parsing its
output.

.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B "\-i, \-\-initiate"
initiate a connection
.TP
.B "\-t, \-\-terminate"
terminate a connection
.TP
.B "\-R, \-\-rekey"
rekey an SA
.TP
.B "\-d, \-\-redirect"
redirect an IKE_SA
.TP
.B "\-p, \-\-install"
install a trap or shunt policy
.TP
.B "\-U, \-\-uninstall"
uninstall a trap or shunt policy
.TP
.B "\-l, \-\-list\-sas"
list currently active IKE_SAs
.TP
.B "\-P, \-\-list\-pols"
list currently installed policies
.TP
.B "\-b, \-\-load\-authorities"
(re\-)load certification authorities information
.TP
.B "\-L, \-\-list\-conns"
list loaded configurations
.TP
.B "\-B, \-\-list\-authorities"
list loaded certification authorities information
.TP
.B "\-x, \-\-list\-certs"
list stored certificates
.TP
.B "\-A, \-\-list\-pools"
list loaded pool configurations
.TP
.B "\-g, \-\-list\-algs"
list loaded algorithms and their implementation
.TP
.B "\-q, \-\-load\-all"
(re\-)load credentials, pools, authorities and connections
.TP
.B "\-c, \-\-load\-conns"
(re\-)load connection configuration
.TP
.B "\-s, \-\-load\-creds"
(re\-)load credentials
.TP
.B "\-a, \-\-load\-pools"
(re\-)load pool configuration
.TP
.B "\-T, \-\-log"
trace logging output (levels 0 and 1 only)
.TP
.B "\-S, \-\-stats"
show daemon infos and statistics
.TP
.B "\-f, \-\-flush\-certs"
flush cached certificates
.TP
.B "\-r, \-\-reload\-settings"
reload strongswan.conf(5) configuration
.TP
.B "\-V, \-\-version"
show daemon version information
.TP
.B "\-h, \-\-help"
show usage, version and plugin information
.SH GENERAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B "\-v, \-\-debug"
set debug level, default: 1
.TP
.B "\-+, \-\-options"
read command line options from file
.TP
.B "\-u, \-\-uri"
service URI to connect to
.SH DIRECTORIES
Credentials are automatically loaded from the following directories by the
\fI\-\-load\-creds\fR command. Files may be encoded in PEM or DER format.

In order to load encrypted files, the password has to be configured in
an appropriate section in \fIswanctl.conf\fR. If no password is found,
\fI\-\-load\-creds\fR will prompt the user for the password unless it is
called with \fI\-\-noprompt\fR.
.TP
.B x509
Trusted X.509 end entity certificates. May be PEM-encoded certificate bundles
(e.g. a full trust chain), see the note regarding bundles below for details.
.TP
.B x509ca
Trusted X.509 Certificate Authority (CA) certificates. May be PEM-encoded
certificate bundles (e.g. a full trust chain), see the note regarding bundles
below for details.
.TP
.B x509aa
Trusted X.509 Attribute Authority (AA) certificates.
.TP
.B x509ocsp
Trusted X.509 OCSP signer certificates. Note that placing a certificate in this
directory explicitly applies the OCSPSigning flag to the certificate even if
it doesn't encode it in its Extended Key Usage extension (EKU).
.TP
.B x509crl
Certificate revocation lists (CRL).
.TP
.B x509ac
Attribute certificates (AC).
.TP
.B pubkey
Raw public keys.
.TP
.B rsa
PKCS#1-encoded RSA private keys.
.TP
.B ecdsa
Plain ECDSA private keys.
.TP
.B pkcs8
PKCS#8 encoded private keys of any type.
.TP
.B private
Private keys in any format. If the format is not detected automatically, place
the file in the appropriate directory above.
.TP
.B pkcs12
PKCS#12 containers from which all certificates and private keys are loaded. Only
files with a single password are supported.
.PP
Additionally, the default \fIswanctl.conf\fR file contains an
\fBinclude conf.d/*.conf\fR statement to load files from the following
directory:
.TP
.B conf.d
May contain config snippets (\fI*.conf\fR files) that are merged with the main
\fIswanctl.conf\fR file.
.SS PEM-encoded Certificate Bundles
In some directories, PEM-encoded certificate bundles are supported (i.e. files
that concatenate several PEM-encoded certificates). This may be used to
load certificate chains from a single file. However, please be aware that for
all other uses, such as referencing a file in \fBcerts\fR or \fBcacerts\fR in
\fIswanctl.conf\fR, only the \fBfirst\fR certificate is loaded from such a file.
So if necessary, structure your files accordingly or split them up.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR swanctl.conf (5)
